      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WORTHTHEADMISSION (8) found 1000m way too short when resuming last start at the Gold Coast. Yet to do anything of note but is in good hands and should appreciate an extra 400m today in this ordinary affair. ANDERLYN (4) has been safely held in two runs this time in work. Did pass quite a few in the straight last time over this trip at Grafton but still beaten a long way. Suited by the small field and the addition of winkers may be significant. JIEBA (1) is a first starter by Street Boss who was in the placings in a recent Ballina trial. Won't need to be a world beater to open the account here. REEL PATIENCE (2) is a Highland Reel six-year-old having his first start. Has obviously had his issues so it might be better to see what he can do before diving in.",
